From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "A.Cervantez" <155030226+Ywach404@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:47:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: step a highlight through dialogue answers with the
 pad

The dialogue HUD has no highlight and answers only to the number keys,
so 0016 put answers 1 to 4 on fixed stick directions. That bakes the
game's four answer cut-off into the controls, and the plan is to lift
it once the game is first person. A list selector does not care how
many answers there are.

In dialogue mode the right stick's up and down flicks and the d-pad
move a highlight through answers 0 to count-1, clamped. Nothing is
highlighted when a dialogue opens, and the first move marks the first
answer. A held step repeats after 0.4 s and then every 0.15 s; the
stick still has to centre after a dialogue opens before it can move
anything. Left, right and the stick's side flicks do nothing.

The highlight is drawn by the game: the chosen slot's text (narrow,
NUL terminated, 0x800 bytes at +0x122C + i*0x800) gets "> " in front,
and sub_10553B50 formats every slot with "%d. %s" each frame, so the
mark shows on the next frame. The whole block is saved first and put
back the moment the highlight moves, clears or is confirmed, but only
while the slot still holds exactly what was written; if the game wrote
the slot since, its text is kept. The edits run in the input pump on
the game thread, between frames. Each pump the count, the four slot
texts and their type and flag words are compared with a snapshot, and
any change other than ours (or history, single line, close, or the HUD
going away) ends the highlight. The marked slot rewritten to its own
text gets the mark again.

Cross and RT confirm: the text goes back first, so the line the game
copies into its history is the answer's own, then the number key is
pressed and released. The game drops a pick within 0.5 s of the last
(its time at +0x5A80); a change there is taken as a pick, and a
confirm inside that window is held and keeps the mark. With nothing
highlighted Cross is still space, the game's continue, and RT sends
nothing, so it no longer opens the history. Circle clears the mark, or
is Escape when there is none. Stepping follows the count the game
reports; a slot past the four the game stores is not written, and a
key past the four Key_Event takes is refused rather than picking the
wrong answer.

These are pad targets, so controls.txt keeps working: answerup,
answerdown, answer and answerclear, the last two with an optional
/fallback. The log reports "dialogue highlight N of M" on change, at
most every 0.25 s while moving, and each confirm, hold and clear.

The input self test drives a fake HUD in guest memory through every
path: stepping and clamping, repeat timing, the prefix applied and
restored on move, clear, confirm, close, history, count change and
external rewrite, the confirm key and the guard, RT not clicking, and
Circle's two meanings.
